caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"DEN","distance":0.7141,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Sean Payton"},{"season":2023,"team":"CIN","distance":0.769,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Zac Taylor"},{"season":2025,"team":"KC","distance":0.7709,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Andy Reid"},{"season":2025,"team":"TEN","distance":0.8478,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Brian Callahan"}],"defense":[{"season":2024,"team":"LA","distance":0.1113,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Chris Shula"},{"season":2025,"team":"TEN","distance":0.1995,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Dennard Wilson"},{"season":2025,"team":"HOU","distance":0.2513,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Matt Burke"},{"season":2022,"team":"DAL","distance":0.2529,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Dan Quinn"},{"season":2025,"team":"BAL","distance":0.2836,"shared":4,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Steelers are 6-3 through week 10 of the 2026 season and have outscored opponents 198 to 182. The offense ranks 18th in EPA per play and the defense 11th in EPA allowed, so neither side has stood out much yet. Their most distinctive trait is the 2nd highest screen rate in the league.","offense":"The Steelers offense has been about average by EPA per play so far, and it has been much better running the ball than passing it. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Their biggest outliers in how they line up are the 2nd highest screen rate and the 3rd highest RPO rate in the league. Aaron Rodgers has run the passing game, with DK Metcalf leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Steelers defense has been a little above average by EPA allowed per play so far. It has been much better against the run than the pass, ranking 5th and 16th. Alex Highsmith has been as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise is Patrick Queen, who has 3.5 sacks, after doing little as a pass rusher a year ago. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is a blitz rate that ranks 11th lowest in the league.","special":"The Steelers have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 79% of field goals, which is a little below average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into linebackers, about 31% of the money on the books. Their linebackers were among the oldest in the league.","players":"Aaron Rodgers has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 2,014 yards. DK Metcalf has been the clear top target with 24% of the looks and 432 receiving yards. Jaylen Warren has handled most of the work in the backfield with 64% of the carries. On defense, T.J. Watt leads the team with 7.5 sacks.","coaching":"Mike McCarthy is calling the offense as head coach and Patrick Graham is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2024 Seahawks and the 2025 Broncos under Sean Payton. Their defense looks most like the 2024 Rams under Chris Shula and the 2025 Titans under Dennard Wilson.","trends":"The offense went from 16th in EPA per play in 2025 to 18th so far this season, about where it was. The defense moved from 18th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 11th so far this season, a modest improvement. The biggest change in approach was two point attempt rate, which went from 4% to 15%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}